      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): strip attachments >10MB before send to prevent HTTP 413 silent message loss (fixes #99021)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99021.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n- Pre-flight size check in sendDiscordMedia strips attachments > 10 MB and sends text-only fallback\n- DEFAULT_MEDIA_MAX_MB restored to 100 so loadMedia can handle oversized files before the send cap\n- Remaining text chunks sent as follow-ups after the fallback\n\n## Evidence (2026-07-02T12:21:25Z, commit: ef35431c54)\n\n### Real Discord API proof (live bot)\n```\nBEFORE: 11MB file -> HTTP 413 -> message lost\nAFTER:  Size check -> text delivered, no attachment\n  HTTP 201, Message ID: 1522195816796782666\n  Content: Check this video..._Attachment exceeds the 10 MB limit_\n  Attachments: 0\n```\n\n### Unit tests (47/47 passed)\n- strips oversized media >10MB and sends text-only fallback\n- respects configured mediaMaxMb above Discord limit\n- sends text-only fallback with long reply text\n- uploads media attachments, uses configured mediaMaxMb\n\n## AI Assistance\n\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
